  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urban and Regional Cooperation with High Income Countries and other key partners in Asia/Pacific  &#xBF; &#xBF;UrbanHICs+</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this new phase of urban diplomacy action, cities and regions will build upon the experiences and lessons learned under the International Urban Cooperation (IUC), the International Urban and Regional Cooperation (IURC) and the International City Partnerships Acting for Green Inclusive Recovery (ICP-AGIR) projects.The &#xBF;UrbanHICs+&#xBF; action will drive &quot;City-to-City Cooperation for Sustainable Urban Development&quot; between the EU and Australia, New Zealand, India, Japan, Republic of Korea, Singapore, Malaysia as well as China, Hong Kong and Taiwan.It will consolidate ongoing regional exchanges in China and Japan and expand &quot;Region-to-Region Cooperation for Sustainable Smart Specialisation&quot; between the EU and Australia and between the EU and the Republic of Korea (RoK).Finally, the action will mainstream academic and business cooperation to consolidate and improve knowledge enhancement and consolidation and research and innovation in support of all partnerships.</narrative>
  </description>
